WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:05.410
Video games are great fun, except for those
occasional moments when they totally stink.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:09.320
Is there anything worse than playing an awesome
game only to have it totally derailed by a

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.590
single moment of pure idiocy?

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:15.790
Here's a look at some video games almost ruined
by one cutscene.

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:16.939
Sonic the Hedgehog

00:00:16.939 --> 00:00:22.330
One of the biggest facepalms in videogame
history took place in 2006's Sonic the Hedgehog,

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:27.410
thanks to the infamous kiss between Princess
Elise and Sonic taking center stage at the

00:00:27.410 --> 00:00:28.689
Cringe Olympics.

00:00:28.689 --> 00:00:33.600
Nonsensical plot developments are usually
fine, especially in a fun platformer like

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.170
this, quotation marks on the "fun," but this
weird fanfic romance between a human and a

00:00:38.170 --> 00:00:40.880
hedgehog was just a little bizarre.

00:00:50.190 --> 00:00:52.260
Super Mario Bros. 2

00:00:52.260 --> 00:00:56.580
There's no denying Super Mario Bros. 2 is
an insanely fun classic.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:01.210
The many different worlds and enemies in this
title gave it loads of character, and players

00:01:01.210 --> 00:01:06.149
can have a great time digging up sand, throwing
eggs back at Birdo, and piloting supporting

00:01:06.149 --> 00:01:08.749
characters like Toad and Princess Peach.

00:01:08.749 --> 00:01:12.999
But then you get to the end and, well, this
happens.

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.539
Yes, it was all a dream.

00:01:17.539 --> 00:01:21.010
Congratulations, you just completely wasted
your time!

00:01:21.010 --> 00:01:22.439
Saints Row the Third

00:01:22.439 --> 00:01:27.520
Considering you can fire octopi onto people's
heads to make them dance, the silly and slapsticky

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:31.469
Saints Row the Third seems like just a goofy,
over the top joyride.

00:01:31.469 --> 00:01:32.920
And usually it is.

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:38.909
That's why it's so jarring when beloved character
Johnny Gat abruptly gets offed during a mission.

00:01:38.909 --> 00:01:42.700
"Johnny, we're about to jump!"

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:45.940
"Hang on, I'll see you at ---"

00:01:48.260 --> 00:01:50.080
Talk about a total mood killer!

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.139
Bayonetta

00:01:51.139 --> 00:01:54.100
There's fanservice, and there's just weird
ickiness.

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:59.229
That lined wasn't blurred so much as obliterated
at the end of the action classic Bayonetta,

00:01:59.229 --> 00:02:04.399
where victorious gamers are treated to a three
minute dance number called "Let's Dance Boys"

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:08.720
featuring the titular heroine just... flouncing
around for your enjoyment.

00:02:16.780 --> 00:02:21.140
Don't worry, it's totally natural to feel
ashamed after playing this game.

00:02:21.150 --> 00:02:22.709
Kingdom Hearts 2

00:02:22.709 --> 00:02:27.180
At least the dance sequence in Kingdom Hearts
2 has one thing going for it: there's no sign

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.209
of Bayonetta.

00:02:28.209 --> 00:02:32.280
But that's the only good thing we can say
about the horrible "Swim This Way" musical

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:36.460
number that features Sora dancing with the
cast of The Little Mermaid.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:42.480
No.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.480
Just… no.

00:02:43.820 --> 00:02:46.140
The Legend of Zelda: Skyward Sword

00:02:46.150 --> 00:02:50.680
There's a lot to love in the classic Zelda
game Skyward Sword…but there's also Groose.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:55.410
For whatever reason, this caricature of a
bully from an '80s shows up and chases down

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:58.020
Link after descending from Skyloft.

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:02.939
Then players have to sit through several minutes
of Groose grunting and hooting about himself,

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.580
his new world, and all sorts of other annoying
crap.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:18.500
Just let us get on with saving Zelda already!

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:20.269
Star Ocean 4

00:03:20.269 --> 00:03:25.079
Get ready to scratch your noggin in confusion
at one of the most awkward cutscenes of all

00:03:25.079 --> 00:03:28.879
time, courtesy of Star Ocean 4's "Private
Action" system.

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:34.329
These are cutscenes you can trigger to raise
your affection level with specific party members.

00:03:34.329 --> 00:03:39.409
That's fine, but the creepily childlike Lymle,
who is actually 15 years old, gets a little

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:40.810
too affectionate.

00:03:48.500 --> 00:03:52.640
Even the other characters in the game are
visibly uncomfortable with how creepy she

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:55.489
is, and send her off to her own room instead.

00:03:55.489 --> 00:03:56.489
Yikes.

00:03:56.489 --> 00:03:57.840
Thanks for watching!

00:03:57.840 --> 00:04:00.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.299
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

